TI  - CELLULAR-DISTRIBUTION OF OMEGA-3 (PERIPHERAL TYPE BENZODIAZEPINE) BINDING-SITES IN THE NORMAL AND ISCHEMIC RAT-BRAIN - AN AUTORADIOGRAPHIC STUDY WITH THE PHOTOAFFINITY LIGAND [H-3] PK-14105
T2  - NEUROSCIENCE LETTERS
AB  - The microscopic distribution of .LAMBDA.3 (peripheral type benzodiazepine) binding sites in sections from normal and ischaemic rat brain has been determined by emulsion autoradiography with the photoaffinity ligand [3H]HP 14105. In the normal rat brain, high densities of .OMEGA.3 sites were present in the ependymal cells, the apical pole of the secretory cells in the choroid plexus and astrocyte-like cells in the outer cellular layer of the olfactory bulb. In ischaemic brain lesions caused by middle cerebral artery occlusion in spontaneously hypertensive rats or in spontaneous ischaemic and haemorrhagic lesions in spontaneously hypertensive stroke-prone rats, the proliferating .OMEGA.3 sites were associated with reactive glial cells and macrophages.
